MID_EV11_073_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_073_m01_001: Attention, please! It's another Anna administrative\nannouncement for the Heroic Games!
MID_EV11_073_m01_002: Hm? Hey, what's different about you? Something's\nnew... Anyway, on to business.
MID_EV11_073_m01_003: Ribeira Winds, are you all set for your next match?\nReally and truly ready?
MID_EV11_073_m01_004: Oh, we're set. You can count on it!
MID_EV11_073_m01_005: Well, that certainly sounds promising. Seems like\nyou're figuring things out.
MID_EV11_073_m01_006: It's been a little while since our last match, but we\nhaven't exactly been taking it easy.
MID_EV11_073_m01_007: Right. We've had quite an adventure.
MID_EV11_073_m01_008: You know, I do see a little more determination on\nyour faces than when we first met.
MID_EV11_073_m01_009: R-really? Hehe. That's nice to hear.
MID_EV11_073_m01_010: Oh... Aren't you from Aurora's temple?
MID_EV11_073_m01_011: Yes. I'm Ultand Serowain. From one temple member\nto another, thank you for your service, Anna.
MID_EV11_073_m01_012: I'm pitching in to help these kids as part of their clan.\nHope you'll cheer us on.
MID_EV11_073_m01_013: Well. I'm sure you have your reasons for doing that.\nAnyway, your next match should be a lot of fun!
MID_EV11_073_m01_014: Speaking of which, I have some details for you.
MID_EV11_073_m01_015: Your next opponents and the day of the match are\nset, so I'm here to give you the info.
MID_EV11_073_m01_016: The details are right here.
MID_EV11_073_m01_017: <TLP>Ribeira Winds\n\nMatch: Third Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Bragança Brotherhood\nLeader: Inyoni\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}　
MID_EV11_073_m01_018: This Inyoni person is quite a big name. I hear she\nexcels with some kind of specially made bow.
MID_EV11_073_m01_019: She's used it to take out some heavy hitters in the\nqualifiers, among other places. Her team is tough.
MID_EV11_073_m01_020: Well, I'm outta here. Make sure you show up on\ntime for your match.
MID_EV11_073_m01_021: Thanks, Anna. We'll be fine.
MID_EV11_073_m01_022: Haaah...
MID_EV11_073_m01_023: Cai, your eyes... Are you sure you're OK? You're not\nfeeling strange at all?
MID_EV11_073_m01_024: I'm good. My eye color changed, but everything else\nseems the same.
MID_EV11_073_m01_025: Since they match my grandma Yu Phas's eyes,\nthey feel kind of comforting.
MID_EV11_073_m01_026: Still... I might be imagining it, but I feel like the\njewel's power has gotten a little stronger.
MID_EV11_038_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_038_m01_001: Looks like everyone's here. I guess you're fighting\nwith us this time. Good to meet you.
MID_EV11_038_m01_002: Hmm, I do see some familiar faces.
MID_EV11_038_m01_027: 
MID_EV11_038_m01_003: Well, well... We meet again! If that's not fate, I don't\nknow what is.
MID_EV11_038_m01_004: You seem to grow more beautiful the more time\nI spend looking. How do you manage that?
MID_EV11_038_m01_005: They say my mother was a true beauty. Just like you,\nshe turned heads wherever she went.
MID_EV11_038_m01_006: She even played the vihuela. Perhaps I've mentioned\nthat already.
MID_EV11_038_m01_007: For someone with such a beautiful mother, you\nturned out so ordinary looking. It's a shame.
MID_EV11_038_m01_008: If you see me every day, you may feel otherwise. So,\nwhy not take this chance to begin our courtship?
MID_EV11_038_m01_009: Spare me, Mr. Big-Shot Merchant. As though I'd\nhave any interest in a fork-tongued flirt like you.
MID_EV11_038_m01_010: Maybe I should relieve you of that tongue entirely.\nI might like you more if you couldn't speak.
MID_EV11_038_m01_011: A lovely offer, but I'll pass. A silver tongue is a tool\nI require for my trade, you see.
MID_EV11_038_m01_012: Oh, uh... I'm Cai, from the village of Ribeira. Great to\nbe working with you all.
MID_EV11_038_m01_013: I'm Talimun, merchant and adventurer of some\nsuccess and renown. A pleasure, Cai.
MID_EV11_038_m01_014: My name is Leda. I'm a vihuela player, as you may\nhave noticed.
MID_EV11_038_m01_015: Now that I've had a good look at you, Cai—oh, you're\njust so adorable. I'm dying to give you a squeeze!
MID_EV11_038_m01_016: Listen, lady. Cai's not interested in that kind of\nthing. Got it?
MID_EV11_038_m01_017: I see you have a nosy little bodyguard. Too bad—\nI was hoping to get to know you better.
MID_EV11_038_m01_018: Leda's an interesting person, huh? She's so beautiful\nand nice and...
MID_EV11_038_m01_019: she kinda smells good...
MID_EV11_038_m01_020: Good gods, Cai! Pull your jaw off the ground!
MID_EV11_038_m01_021: What's a kid like you doing in a tournament like this?\nIsn't it a bit dangerous for someone your age?
MID_EV11_038_m01_022: These games pull in all the best fighters from across\nthe Dagdan Empire. You slip up, it's all over for you.
MID_EV11_038_m01_023: Well, my dad's locked up in the dungeon. I need to\nwin so I can get him released.
MID_EV11_038_m01_024: Then me, my dad, and my mom can live together like\na family.
MID_EV11_038_m01_025: Hmm... Like a family, huh?
MID_EV11_038_m01_026: Whew. That's rough, kid. Good luck out there.
MID_EV11_074_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_074_m01_001: Good patrons of the games! Surely you are all\nfamiliar with the legendary Battle of Zol!
MID_EV11_074_m01_002: The year is 663 by the Imperial Calendar. The Lydia,\na powerful, war-like people, ruled the land of Zol!
MID_EV11_074_m01_003: The young hero Arago sets out to seize the territory,\nunder direct orders from Dagda the Great!
MID_EV11_074_m01_004: Standing in the way is the great Devil Mountain\nof Zol.
MID_EV11_074_m01_005: The welcome for heroic Arago and his troops?\nPoisoned arrows raining down from the mount!
MID_EV11_074_m01_006: To the east, representing the Arago elite! An array\nof dazzling fighters from every corner of Dagda!
MID_EV11_074_m01_007: To the west, representing the fighters of the Lydia!\nThe well-known Bragança Brotherhood!
MID_EV11_074_m01_008: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV11_074_m01_009: I will kill them all. Anyone who stands in my way.\nKill them.
MID_EV11_074_m01_010: The voice... It says... Destroy everything...
MID_EV11_074_m01_011: You must be Magic-Bow Inyoni. Quite the celebrity\nright now, aren't you?
MID_EV11_074_m01_012: You made a real name for yourself as an archer. But\nI've gotta say, something's a bit odd about you.
MID_EV11_074_m01_013: You wouldn't want to sell me that bow, would you?\nI'll give you a good deal.
MID_EV11_074_m01_014: Nng...
MID_EV11_074_m01_015: Well, we can talk business after the fight if you like.\nYou think it over.
MID_EV11_074_m01_016: Talimun.
MID_EV11_074_m01_017: Do you think Inyoni's bow could be one of \nDrake's treasures?
MID_EV11_074_m01_018: Oho? I'm surprised someone your age knows\nabout those.
MID_EV11_074_m01_019: But yes—you're right. I've heard a few rumors.
MID_EV11_074_m01_020: That thing is called Ugo's Bow, and it's supposedly\npowerful enough to pierce any material.
MID_EV11_074_m01_021: Yeah, but I'd bet the real danger is that other woman\njust behind her.
MID_EV11_074_m01_022: Cai... Is that...
MID_EV11_074_m01_023: Yes. She was in the ruined fort.
MID_EV11_074_m01_024: Tch...
MID_EV11_074_m01_025: Was she the one trying to steal the red jewel from\nyour house?
MID_EV11_074_m01_026: Not exactly. I mean, she was behind the thieves,\npulling the strings.
MID_EV11_074_m01_027: Interesting. The plot thickens. She must have\nsome strong influence.
MID_EV11_074_m01_028: 
MID_EV11_039_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_039_m01_001: Well done, everyone. It feels good to win a match,\ndoesn't it?
MID_EV11_039_m01_028: 
MID_EV11_039_m01_002: You and your friends did some great work out there,\nCai. I was impressed.
MID_EV11_039_m01_003: Thanks! You were great too, Leda.
MID_EV11_039_m01_004: I agree. So cool under pressure. I have to say, I've\ncome to respect you.
MID_EV11_039_m01_005: You know, ladies... I did some work out there too.
MID_EV11_039_m01_006: You think so? If you ask me, Mr. Big-Shot Merchant\ncould have put in more effort.
MID_EV11_039_m01_007: Oho! No mercy, eh? Don't you think you're being just\na tad harsh?
MID_EV11_039_m01_008: {SetColor=Gray}They act like they've been through a war together...\nHow long can that last, I wonder.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_039_m01_009: {SetColor=Gray}Only one clan can win in the end.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_039_m01_010: {SetColor=Gray}If we each keep winning, we're guaranteed to have\nto face one another before this is over.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_039_m01_011: {SetColor=Gray}This isn't the last we'll see of each other. But now\nI've seen you fight, so I'll be ready.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_039_m01_012: By the way, what kind of request will you make if\nyou win the tournament, Leda?
MID_EV11_039_m01_013: Let me guess... You think a girl like me couldn't\npossibly have a reason to compete in the games.
MID_EV11_039_m01_014: Oh, but I do have a reason and a request. Trite as it\nmight sound, I will ask for revenge.
MID_EV11_039_m01_015: What? What do you mean?
MID_EV11_039_m01_016: The man who killed my father is here in Dagsion,\nin a place I can't get to.
MID_EV11_039_m01_017: If I win—when I win—I'll have him brought to me.\nAnd then I'll plunge a dagger into his chest.
MID_EV11_039_m01_018: You see, I can't let anyone stand in the way of my\nvictory. Not anyone.
MID_EV11_039_m01_019: I think it's time to go. But I'm sure we'll meet\nagain soon.
MID_EV11_039_m01_020: And when we do, we'll be enemies. See ya then, kids.
MID_EV11_039_m01_021: Leda's kind of scary.
MID_EV11_039_m01_022: Yeah, I wasn't expecting that. She was pretty good at\nhiding her real thoughts...until now.
MID_EV11_039_m01_023: I guess everyone has heavy burdens to carry.
MID_EV11_039_m01_024: Hey, did Talimun leave?! When did that happen?
MID_EV11_039_m01_025: He slipped out a while ago. He's another one I don't\nquite understand.
MID_EV11_039_m01_027: He slipped out a while ago. He's another one I don't\nquite understand.
MID_EV11_039_m01_026: Does Talimun have a goal that he can't let go of\ntoo? I guess he must.
MID_EV11_040_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_040_m01_001: Ah. Pardon the intrusion.
MID_EV11_040_m01_002: This was the anteroom assigned to Inyoni's clan,\nbut they appear to have left already.
MID_EV11_040_m01_003: Looks like they left her behind. She's in rough shape.\nI'm not even sure she hears us.
MID_EV11_040_m01_004: Haaah... Ngh...
MID_EV11_040_m01_005: There's no reason for us to linger here. The bow\nwe're looking for must be long gone at this point.
MID_EV11_040_m01_006: Hm. One loss, and they leave you high and dry, huh?\nThat's just heartless.
MID_EV11_040_m01_007: Well... I didn't catch every detail in the Order's little\nchat earlier, but I think I get what happened here.
MID_EV11_040_m01_008: Hey, there! Can you hear me? Let's see if you still\nremember your name.
MID_EV11_040_m01_009: Inyoni...
MID_EV11_040_m01_010: Ah! There you are! I need to ask you a question\nor two, Inyoni.
MID_EV11_040_m01_011: That bow you had... I'm sure you know it's\nno normal weapon. Where'd you get it?
MID_EV11_040_m01_012: Got it...through the Order of Mithras... Paid a lot of\nmoney for it...
MID_EV11_040_m01_013: Sounds about right. And that Hong Hua woman\nis part of the Order of Mithras as well.
MID_EV11_040_m01_014: She was...acting as my...assistant in the tournament...
MID_EV11_040_m01_015: Assistant. Right. I wager she only wanted to keep an\neye on you.
MID_EV11_040_m01_016: Drake's treasures are powerful, but they tend to eat\naway at their users' minds over time.
MID_EV11_040_m01_017: You start to hear voices coming from the treasure\nand everything, or so they say.
MID_EV11_040_m01_018: Voices? Do...you hear these voices?
MID_EV11_040_m01_019: Well, not me, no. Though rumor is that they sound\nlike a song—a dirge of hate.
MID_EV11_040_m01_020: What could the Order be planning, doling out\nweapons with such terrible power?
MID_EV11_040_m01_021: Who knows. I somehow doubt their goal was to prop\nthis lot up and win the tournament.
MID_EV11_040_m01_022: And until we can ask the puppet masters directly,\nI doubt we'll find out.
MID_EV11_040_m01_023: But hey, good news. You're not too far gone, Inyoni.\nYou'll be back to your old self in no time.
MID_EV11_040_m01_024: If you're disappointed with the outcome here, at least\nnow you know to avoid such dangerous artifacts.
MID_EV11_040_m01_025: Oh, and steer clear of nefarious types like the Order\nof Mithras. Both good lessons to learn.
MID_EV11_041_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_041_m01_001: I'm sorry, but I have no clue about manners and how\nto behave in situations like this.
MID_EV11_041_m01_002: I don't mind. Please don't concern yourself about it.\nSet your heart at ease.
MID_EV11_041_m01_003: With your last victory, you advance to the main\nmatches. Congratulations are in order.
MID_EV11_041_m01_004: I saw how well you fought in the qualifiers.
MID_EV11_041_m01_005: It seems great power is at your command. And\nwhat's more, you're blessed with good friends.
MID_EV11_041_m01_006: Your victories were no accident. At your young age,\nsuccess like this is quite an accomplishment.
MID_EV11_041_m01_007: This might sound odd, but... Have we met before?
MID_EV11_041_m01_008: I'm pretty sure this is the first time.
MID_EV11_041_m01_009: The hue of your eyes reminds me of my wife. It's a\nwonder you're not related somehow.
MID_EV11_041_m01_010: Your deeds have caught my interest. And I wondered\nwhat it is that you hope to have granted if you win.
MID_EV11_041_m01_040: <NCA>Explain your wish.
MID_EV11_041_m01_011: What I want is... Well, my father is locked up in a\ndungeon here. He's going to be executed.
MID_EV11_041_m01_012: I want to win so I can request that he's spared.
MID_EV11_041_m01_013: But things are changing. At the moment, I'd like it if\nyou, Lord Solel, would speak with my mother.
MID_EV11_041_m01_014: Is that really all you want? That modest request?
MID_EV11_041_m01_015: Yes, I'd like you to grant my mother's wish. Really,\nshe and I want the same thing.
MID_EV11_041_m01_016: Very well. If you win the tournament, I will grant\nyour wish.
MID_EV11_041_m01_017: Uhm... I hope this isn't rude, but... May I ask you\nabout your family?
MID_EV11_041_m01_018: The mortal notion of family is a little different than\nthe one held by those of us called gods.
MID_EV11_041_m01_019: The most important difference is in the perception\nof time.
MID_EV11_041_m01_020: A god's lifespan can be many times that of a mortal's.
MID_EV11_041_m01_021: But that can feel more like a cage than a blessing.\nAt least, sometimes we think of it that way.
MID_EV11_041_m01_022: I do have those I would consider family. My departed\nwife, for example, and the daughter we had together.
MID_EV11_041_m01_023: Lord Solel... Your daughter, Aurora, is locked up in\nthe temple. I heard you won't meet with her...
MID_EV11_041_m01_024: That's the rumor, anyway. But is it true?
MID_EV11_041_m01_025: What I mean is... Is that the right way to treat\nyour daughter?
MID_EV11_041_m01_027: Aurora? I... I need more time to properly speak\nwith...her.
MID_EV11_041_m01_028: I've stumbled into a situation that requires me to\nkeep her at a distance.
MID_EV11_041_m01_029: But that is a family matter. Strangers such as you\nshould not intrude.
MID_EV11_041_m01_030: But what if the person who wins the games asks you\nto go and talk to Aurora?
MID_EV11_041_m01_031: Is that a wish you would grant?
MID_EV11_041_m01_032: If that is truly what they desired, then I would give\nit some thorough consideration.
MID_EV11_041_m01_033: Ah...
MID_EV11_041_m01_034: You intrigue me. As to your wish, you ought to take\na little more time considering it.
MID_EV11_041_m01_035: Perhaps a new wish will arise. We'll call your current\nwish a provisional one.
MID_EV11_041_m01_038: I understand, and I'll think about it. Thank you.
MID_EV11_041_m01_039: Fascinating child. Earnest and forthright—no doubt\nrighteously raised by excellent parents.